{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "All work is performed inside the existing Spring XD multi-module Gradle codebase, following its established module plugin SPI, test conventions (JUnit + Spring integration tests) and CI (Jenkins) setup.",
    "U1 (Reactor processor plugin): Implement a Reactor processor module type following the same module-plugin pattern already used for Spark/RxJava modules; the minimal required metadata is the processor class name; additional configuration is exposed through standard module option metadata so it can be set with the known module option commands.",
    "U2 (Reactor 2.0 RC1 upgrade): Bump the Reactor version in the central Gradle dependency management, align transitive dependencies to the versions required by RC1, and adapt XD code to breaking Reactor 2.0 API changes (e.g., Streams/Promise changes) with the smallest possible refactoring; no architectural redesign.",
    "U3/U4 (Redis field-value counter aggregation): Use Spring Data Redis (RedisTemplate) with atomic Redis hash/counter operations (HINCRBY or a Lua script) so aggregation can be written continuously during ingestion; port the previous aggregate field-value counter spec, fill identified gaps, and update the reference documentation.",
    "U5 (Hadoop test isolation): Create a dedicated Gradle subproject for Hadoop-dependent tests, move them out of the DIRT project, remove the Hadoop dependencies from DIRT, and fix the Eclipse classpath file generation.",
    "U6 (XD+YARN on EC2 acceptance tests): Provide provisioning scripts for a small YARN cluster on EC2, implement acceptance tests covering simple XD features (stream deployment, basic source/sink processing) running on YARN, and hook the suite into the nightly CI build cycle rather than the per-commit build.",
    "U7 (RxJava processor module): Implement an RxJava-based processor module using the same module SPI as in U1 so users can supply RxJava (Observable-based) computation logic for stream processing.",
    "U8 (HTTP source message size): Expose the currently hard-coded 1MB HttpChunkAggregator limit as a configurable module property, wire it through the server configuration so it can be overridden in servers.yml, and keep 1MB as the default for backward compatibility."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "U3 and U4 are duplicates of the same requirement and are implemented once; effort is counted only once.",
    "The generic Spring Framework 6 / Java 17 preamble is contextual; the increment targets the existing Spring XD platform, its current JDK level, and its existing Gradle build.",
    "One developer performs all work; estimates are ideal engineering workdays (8 hours) of development effort, excluding elapsed calendar effects, release management, and meetings beyond normal development.",
    "Each activity estimate includes its own unit tests; dedicated integration/system test activities are listed separately where relevant; a final cross-story integration and code-review activity is included.",
    "Reactor 2.0 RC1 API changes are limited to what is needed for compilation and runtime compatibility; no redesign of XD stream processing is required.",
    "EC2 credentials/budget and a small YARN test cluster are available for U6; test instability is covered by the stabilization activity.",
    "A Redis instance (embedded or local) is available for development and tests of U3/U4.",
    "Documentation effort covers only the reference documentation and module option docs explicitly mentioned in the stories; no full user-guide rewrite.",
    "Existing Spark/RxJava module support code is available as a template for U1 and U7, reducing design uncertainty.",
    "No clarifications are required; acceptance criteria are derived directly from the story texts and linked PR/wiki references."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Analysis and design of Reactor processor plugin",
      "activity_description": "Analyze existing Spark/RxJava module plugin approach, design the Reactor processor module type, its minimal metadata (processor class) and how module options are declared and set via module option commands.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Implement Reactor processor module support",
      "activity_description": "Implement base classes and module-plugin integration so a Reactor-based stream processor can be deployed by specifying only the processor class; wire into the XD module framework.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Module option configuration support",
      "activity_description": "Implement additional configuration of Reactor processor modules through well-known module option commands, including option metadata and validation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Tests and documentation",
      "activity_description": "Write unit and integration tests for the Reactor processor plugin and document usage and module options.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Reactor 2.0 RC1 dependency upgrade",
      "activity_description": "Update Gradle dependency management to Reactor 2.0 RC1 and align dependent libraries to stable, synchronized versions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Code migration and regression fixes",
      "activity_description": "Fix compilation errors and adapt code to Reactor 2.0 RC1 API changes, run the full test suite and fix regressions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U3/U4 - Port specs and gap analysis",
      "activity_description": "Port the aggregate field-value counter specifications from the previous implementation wiki and identify functional gaps to be covered.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U3/U4 - Implement Redis aggregation over field-value counters",
      "activity_description": "Implement the Redis-backed aggregation store using atomic Redis counter/hash operations so aggregated values are continuously written as data is ingested.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U3/U4 - Integrate aggregation with ingestion pipeline",
      "activity_description": "Wire the Redis aggregation into the stream ingestion path (module/message-bus integration) so counters update continuously at runtime.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U3/U4 - Tests for Redis aggregation",
      "activity_description": "Unit and integration tests (against embedded/local Redis) covering continuous aggregation, restart behavior, and the gaps identified in A7.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "U3/U4 - Reference documentation update",
      "activity_description": "Update the reference documentation describing the Redis-based field-value counter aggregation, options, and behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Create separate Hadoop test project",
      "activity_description": "Create a new Gradle subproject, move Hadoop-dependent tests out of the DIRT project, and adjust dependencies so DIRT no longer depends on Hadoop test artifacts.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Build, CI and Eclipse classpath verification",
      "activity_description": "Verify Gradle and CI builds pass, and confirm Eclipse classpath file generation is correct without the Hadoop dependencies.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "U6 - EC2/YARN test environment provisioning",
      "activity_description": "Create/reuse scripts to provision a small YARN cluster on EC2 and install/configure XD for acceptance testing.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Implement XD-on-YARN acceptance tests",
      "activity_description": "Implement acceptance tests verifying simple XD features (stream creation/deployment, basic source-to-sink processing) running on YARN.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A16",
      "activity_name": "U6 - CI integration and stabilization",
      "activity_description": "Integrate the acceptance suite into the build cycle (nightly CI job), handle environment teardown, and stabilize flaky tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A17",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Implement RxJava processor module",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement the RxJava-based processor module using the module SPI so users can leverage RxJava APIs for data computations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A18",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Tests and documentation for RxJava module",
      "activity_description": "Unit/integration tests for the RxJava processor module plus a usage sample and module documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A19",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Expose HTTP source message-size property",
      "activity_description": "Expose the hard-coded 1MB HttpChunkAggregator limit as a configurable property and wire it through server configuration so it can be overridden via servers.yml; default stays 1MB.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A20",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Tests and documentation for HTTP override",
      "activity_description": "Tests verifying the servers.yml override and default behavior, plus documentation of the new property.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A21",
      "activity_name": "Cross-cutting integration, code review and build verification",
      "activity_description": "Final integration of all stories, self code review cleanup, full multi-module build and regression run, and preparation of the increment for merge.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 56
  }
}
